Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add MXFP4 tests: llama.cpp golden bytes, GGUF round-trip,
 matmul

- tests/mxfp4_tests.rs: two golden blocks generated by compiling llama.cpp's
  quantize_row_mxfp4_ref + ggml_e8m0_to_fp32_half as a standalone C program
  against fixed LCG inputs; asserts byte-identical quantizer output, an
  independent reference decode of dequantize, a GGUF write/read round trip
  (which also exercises dtype id 39 in both directions), and dtype plumbing
  (17 bytes / 32 elements).
- tests/quantized_tests.rs: MXFP4 added to the generic quantized-matmul and
  CPU-embedding coverage. The matmul tolerance is relaxed for MXFP4 (0.15 vs
  0.02) because the E2M1 2-bit mantissa carries far more quantization error
  than any other candle dtype; the bound still catches implementation bugs.
  ggml_reference_matmul_error gains a measured constant (0.032, from the
  ggml harness on x86_64).
